# Air-gapped LAN-only edge (MasterControl).
#
# The K2 daemon stays on loopback (127.0.0.1:60710). This Caddy listen is
# the one TCP port the IDS/firewall monitors. HTTP and WebSocket share it.
#
# Image env (systemd, before first start):
#   K2_AIRGAP=1
# Do not set K2_LISTEN=lan — that would bind the daemon on the LAN too.
#
# Add Server in the K2 client:
#   http://<LAN-IP>:38471
#
# Replace 192.168.1.50 with the box's LAN IP. Bind host:port (not a bare
# :38471) unless you want every interface. Do not use 80, 443, 8080, or
# 8443. If you pick a different high port, change this file and the Add
# Server URL together.
#
# Runbook: .k2/prds/runbook-airgap-linux-image-v1.md

http://192.168.1.50:38471 {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:60710
}
